\section{Leave-One-Session-Out Inflation}\label{sec:loso}

Table~\ref{tab:loso} reports results under the protocol that the contamination affects.
With the released
text features, folds 1--4 score between 88.3\% and 90.2\%, fold 5 scores 59.36\%, and the
five-fold mean is 83.52\% --- 24 points above the standard split. Fusing all three
released blocks, the configuration most papers report, gives a five-fold mean of 83.58\%
against 57.59\%. The visual block alone inflates by 18 points. Unsupervised audio moves
by two points. With frozen text encoders the five-fold mean is \emph{below} the standard
split by 3.8 to 4.8 points (1.5 with BERT text plus released audio), which is what an unbiased estimate would show if session 5 is
the easier test set.

