\section{Feature Provenance and Usage}\label{sec:prov}

We compared, utterance by utterance, the bc-LSTM release with the
\texttt{IEMOCAP\_features.pkl} files shipped by the DialogueGCN and MMGCN code releases
(Table~\ref{tab:prov}, Fig.~\ref{fig:prov}). The DialogueGCN file is identical to the bc-LSTM file in every
block. The MMGCN file keeps the identical text block and replaces the audio and visual
blocks with a 1{,}582-d acoustic descriptor and a 342-d visual descriptor. Utterance ids,
labels and the train/test split are the same in all three. The contaminated text block
therefore reaches every model that reads the text block of any of the three files.
MMGCN's own audio and visual blocks, by contrast, pass the test: under LOSO their five-fold
means sit slightly \emph{below} the standard split (audio 49.45\% against 51.14\%, visual
35.61\% against 36.76\%), and their session gaps are negative ($g=-2.6$ points for audio
and $-6.7$ for visual) while the shared text block in the same file gives $+31.1$. Both
tests thus agree: in the MMGCN file the contamination is confined to the text block.

