\textbf{Saturated model selection.} The same release's CMU-MOSI~\cite{zadeh2016} and
CMU-MOSEI~\cite{zadeh2018} features show the symptom a user can see without any extra
experiment (Table~\ref{tab:sat}). Held-out \emph{training} videos reach 98.9\% text-only
accuracy on MOSI and 99.2\% with fusion, against about 80\% on test, and the label-fit
visual block shows the same pattern. On MOSEI the label-fit blocks do not saturate but
still lose 3 to 12 points from held-out to test, while the unsupervised audio block shows
neither pattern on either corpus. This is the signature of the session gap in a corpus
without sessions. On MOSI, hyperparameter and fusion-style selection on such a held-out
split is close to arbitrary: a practitioner choosing configurations on it is choosing
among near-ties.

